{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["<b>You shall not make a covenant with them or with their gods</b> — He warned that he not make a covenant with them to let live any soul among them. <b>Or with their gods</b> — He warned that he not make a covenant with them to leave their idolatry intact, but rather that he demolish them and smash their pillars. And it is possible that he says: he shall not make a covenant with them and with their gods as one, but rather that he demolish them and smash their pillars. And the intent is to say that while they are still worshipping their gods, he shall not make a covenant with them; but if they accepted upon themselves not to practise idolatry, it is permitted to let them endure."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {0 "The verse phrase וְלֵאלֹהֵיהֶם is repeated in two proposed readings of the verse's syntax; both are rendered literally as Ramban presents them."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:15:21.742713448Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}